<newsitem itemid="82147" id="root" date="1996-09-27" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Chesterton full-year profits drop.</title>
<headline>Chesterton full-year profits drop.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.7		    vs 7.1</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.0		    vs same</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 3.0		    vs same</p>
<p> Pretax		     2.4		    vs 5.3</p>
<p> Turnover		   89.7		   vs 69.3</p>
<p> Operating profit	 3.8		    vs 6.6</p>
<p> Tax			  1.3		    vs 1.5</p>
<p> Net taxed		  1.1		    vs 3.8</p>
<p> Pay date		   Dec 2</p>
<p> Div registration date  Oct 15</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Oct 7</p>
<p>NOTE - Chesterton, a property consultant, said results were hit by unspecified one-off investment costs and accounting write-offs. It added current trading and order levels are strong and that the property market has picked up.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
